---
import IntegrationReadiness from '../IntegrationReadiness.astro';
const capabilities = [
  ['01', 'Reuse your storefront', 'Keep the Shopify or Shopify Plus store where you already manage your supplier catalog. No separate PunchOut storefront is required.'],
  ['02', 'Set buyer access', 'Map each buyer connection to its store and accessible catalog or collections.'],
  ['03', 'Return the cart', 'Send selected items back to the buyer’s procurement system for approval instead of using normal Shopify checkout.'],
  ['04', 'Create the order after approval', 'When the approved purchase order arrives, PunchOut Central creates the corresponding Shopify order.'],
  ['05', 'Manage multiple connections', 'Serve multiple enterprise buyers from one Shopify store, or manage buyer connections across multiple stores.'],
  ['06', 'Follow the transaction', 'View the session, cart, PO, store order, invoice and any issues in one transaction history.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview">
    <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
      <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="ey">Shopify PunchOut integration</span>
        <h1>Make your existing Shopify store a PunchOut supplier catalog.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Connect enterprise buyers to your Shopify or Shopify Plus storefront through PunchOut Central. Buyers shop the catalog you configure for them; their procurement system handles approval.</p>
        <div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss your Shopify setup &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#flow">See the connection &darr;</a><a class="btn shopify-app-badge" href="https://apps.shopify.com/punchout-central" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Install on Shopify <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal">
        <div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Supplier storefront</span><b>Shopify</b></div>
        <div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>Shopify</strong></div>
        <span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span>
        <h3>One catalog, buyer-specific access</h3>
        <p>Use your current store for PunchOut shopping and approved orders.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">Connection roles</span><h2>Shopify is the supplier storefront.</h2><p class="lead">The buyer starts in procurement. PunchOut Central connects that session to the supplier catalog and tracks the transaction.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal">
      <div class="integration-node"><strong>Buyer procurement</strong><span>Starts session and approves cart</span></div>
      <div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Buyer connection and workflow</span></div>
      <div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify / Shopify Plus</strong><span>Supplier catalog and approved order</span></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify connection</span><h2>From buyer-specific catalog to approved store order.</h2><p class="lead">The catalog is available during PunchOut; the order waits for procurement approval.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">{capabilities.map(([number, title, description]) => <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Connection planning</span><h2>Match your store to the buyer’s requirements.</h2><p class="lead">Confirm the buyer’s procurement system, cXML or OCI protocol, catalog access and test process for each connection.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/"><span>Buyer side</span><h3>Procurement systems</h3><p>See the buyer ecosystem and what to verify before connecting.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/cxml/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>cXML PunchOut</h3><p>Learn about cXML catalog and procurement workflows.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/oci/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>OCI PunchOut</h3><p>Learn about OCI launch and cart return.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <IntegrationReadiness platform="shopify" />
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Shopify PunchOut questions</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal">
      <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does PunchOut Central support Shopify?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Shopify and Shopify Plus are live as supplier catalog platforms: buyer launch, catalog shopping, cart return, approved PO to Shopify order, and invoice activity.</p></div></div>
      <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is setup included?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Standard supported integration setup and onboarding are included at no extra charge. Buyer-specific custom development is separate.</p></div></div>
      <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Do we need another storefront?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. PunchOut Central uses the supplier’s existing Shopify or Shopify Plus store as the catalog.</p></div></div>
      <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does cart return create a Shopify order?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. Cart return sends the selection to procurement. The Shopify order follows the approved purchase order.</p></div></div>
      <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Can different buyers use the same store?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Buyer connections can have their own store, collection and catalog access settings.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Connect your catalog</span><h2>Review the buyer and store together.</h2><p class="lead">Bring the procurement requirement and the Shopify store you want to use.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss your integration &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a></div></div></section>
</main>
